            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Thanks for taking a look. I lean towards using both markers with the same priority. `{ '.slang', '.git' }` is prone to the similar problem - in the absence of `.slang` in the repo there is a risk that global user config at `$HOME/.slang/` (if present) will make `$HOME` a workspace root before considering `.git` marker in the repo.",
